    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `customerCode` assignment on owner creation, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**How it works:** In `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the `POST /api/owners` handler), just before persisting a new owner, `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` computes:\n- `LAST3` = first three letters of `lastName`, upper-cased (`Locale.ROOT`)\n- `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits\n\nSince the code is computed and persisted at create time, two successive creates get consecutive sequence numbers (e.g. `SMI-0007` then `JON-0008`), satisfying the global-sequence guarantee.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 assigns the code before `saveOwner`, plus the `nextCustomerCode` helper.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically onto the GET response.\n- `resources/db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (`ddl-auto=none`, so the schema is source-of-truth).\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreFormatAndGlobalSequence`) verifies `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that the two sequence numbers differ by exactly one \u2014 all passing.",
